  "body": "There's a lot to like about 33A Te Arawa Street, and considerably less to do once you're living here. Three double bedrooms plus a study, two levels, generous outdoor space and a north-facing orientation give this home the sort of flexibility that makes family life considerably easier  - while its elevated position brings excellent light, privacy and a lovely sense of separation from the bustle of the neighbourhood. A big home for living large - your immediate exploration is recommended. \r\n\r\nThe main living zone is spacious, open plan and wonderfully connected to the enormous deck. The kitchen sits at the heart of it all, with plenty of bench space and room to bring your own ideas to the table. Throw open the doors, send everyone outside and let the evenings take care of themselves this summer. \r\n\r\nNothing compares to the location - Mission Bay is close enough for a spontaneous swim, dinner out or coffee run, while city access and public transport keep the daily commute nicely under control. This position is all about lifestyle and functional living for ultimate convenience. \r\n\r\n* Three double bedrooms across two levels plus an office\r\n\r\n* Large north-facing deck with covered section\r\n\r\n* Two downstairs bedrooms  + an office, all opening towards the garden\r\n\r\n* Upstairs master suite with ensuite and walk-in wardrobe\r\n\r\n* Flexible downstairs space - bedroom, second lounge, teenagers' retreat or rumpus\r\n\r\n* Generous lawn and fully fenced\r\n\r\n* Elevated position with excellent natural light\r\n\r\n* Weatherboard construction\r\n\r\nThe vendors are ready to move on, which means this is one to take seriously. If you've been waiting for a substantial Orakei  home with genuine space, outdoor living and plenty of options for the future, make 33A Te Arawa Street your next move. You may find the search ends rather sooner than expected.\r\n\r\nWe collaborate with every agency, so if you have buyers that may be interested please call Mike today",
